It's a new archetype, a new form of the hero. And the way I usually define it is as an individual. individual who uses the internet or social media to help other people, animals, or the environment. You described something in your research called collaborative heroism. Can you talk about what that is and how it relates to the rise of social media? Yes. Collaborative heroism is my most recent area of research and really what it is. A lot of people have the idea that people who take action online, there's a nickname that was coined to to refer to that called slacktivist. And so it gives us negative connotation that people who are taking action online are somehow slacking off on taking action in, let's just say, offline,
这是一个新原型，一种新型的英雄。我通常将其定义为一个个人。一个利用互联网或社交媒体来帮助他人、动物或环境的个人。您在研究中描述了一种叫做协作式英雄主义的现象。您能谈谈那是什么，以及它与社交媒体兴起的关系吗？是的。协作式英雄主义是我最近的研究领域，它实际上是这样的。许多人有一种印象，认为在网上采取行动的人，有一个专门指代这种行为的绰号叫“网络懒汉”。因此这给人一种负面印象，即在网上采取行动的人在某种程度上是在逃避在现实中采取行动，比方说，

4
